From 26691e1ce5c15ae56b13a2154d3b1f228916d156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:57:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(core-update): a paused turn continues within 90 s of the
 checkout moving, ahead of automatic turns [daveey]

Live on David-MBP 2026-10-28 17:22 (t_01a18300e42c3364, 2nd attempt): the checkout moved at 17:22:19
on a serve the update left alive; 2 s later a kanban notice claimed the idle paused session, ran 8 min
over the pause and kept the backend busy, and the paused turn only continued from the 300 s backstop
at 17:30:39 (502 s after the gateway was back).

- From the end of the window until the continuation records its marker, automatic turns
  (_notif_claim_turn: kanban notices, process completions, /loop, heartbeats, wake-ups) are refused
  and requeue (update_pause.continuation_due). Read live while a watcher runs; bounded by DUE_HOLD_S
  past the last poll, KICKOFF_HOLD_S after scheduling (agent build) and HOLD_MAX_S past the window end.
- Every hand-off bound counts from the first sight of the move, including while a synthesized turn
  runs over the pause (new "carried" action), so a flipping outlook or a carried turn never restarts it.
- An outlook that says "coming" but never begins retiring (no RetirementFence.retiring()) within
  HANDOFF_WAIT_S (90 s, two skew polls + margin) continues here; blocked still at 60 s; retiring
  keeps the hand-off (the fence refuses in-place work).
- Each outlook change is logged, so the next live window shows the decision path.
